           with content="Local KVM parity recovery commit prepared; not pushed or published.\n\nRepository: rrnewton/reverie\nBranch: codex/kvm-pr611-recovery-20260922\nBase: 8c867cbb3cfdacbec0f825478d1f62b5cac3744b\nCommit: d96682882cedfe89aa05914bad4fcbd1eb0ea75a\nTree: 7ef74e96a324291f9b82ae4fe89c2ef6606a1710\nAuthor and committer: rrnewton-bots <330061689+rrnewton-bots@users.noreply.github.com>\nCommit body begins with: [hermit2, degraded-unresolved, gpt-5.6-sol, devbig014, role=impl]\n\nBehavior:\n- KVM fchdir now consumes the Linux low 32-bit fd word.\n- Ordinary O_PATH directory descriptors are accepted, including dup and proc-fd-reopened aliases.\n- The cwd is held by an independent private descriptor, so source close does not break later relative lookup.\n- Captured stdout and stderr resolve through private capture carriers; physical supervisor fd 1 and 2 directories are never used as guest cwd.\n- Non-directories are classified before the fallible retained-cwd reopen, preserving ENOTDIR rather than leaking host EMFILE for regular files, pipes, and captured FIFOs.\n- Synthetic proc-root fchdir remains refused with EACCES.\n- README capability text now matches behavior.\n\nExact review artifact:\n- ignored/recovery/fchdir-opath-20260922/fchdir-frozen-v5.diff\n- SHA-256 26e5fe121d1c70d134711041d7a966879d8b8556bf5c9a8e53feb575913864f7\n- 15,079 bytes, 360 lines\n- Commit diff is byte-identical to the reviewed artifact.\n\nAdversarial review:\n- Three independent reviewers approved exact frozen v5 with no findings.\n- Goalpost checks: no weakened assertion, widened tolerance, new exemption, skipped case, relaxed comparator, relabelled failure, or deleted semantic check.\n- Earlier v1-v4 findings were fixed before v5: unrelated proc-root stdout comparison, no-op cwd positive fixture, non-causative high-word call, stale README text, and fd-exhaustion errno ordering.\n\nValidation on exact v5:\n- cargo test -p reverie-kvm --lib: 882 passed in 7.85 seconds.\n- cargo test -p reverie-kvm --lib -- --test-threads=1: 882 passed in 28.93 seconds.\n- cargo clippy -p reverie-kvm --all-targets -- -D warnings: passed in 5.76 seconds.\n- fchdir unit group: 3 passed, including injected-EMFILE negative and qualifying arms.\n- Required-KVM focused parity cell passed three outer repetitions; every test invocation runs native once, direct KVM twice, and CounterTool KVM twice with exact output, exit, and stderr equality.\n- Required-KVM captured-dirfd physical-fd-reuse cell passed.\n- Proc-root cwd case 6 passed and now removes the prior KVM O_PATH exemption.\n- Unrelated proc-root statfs policy control passed.\n- Required-KVM anti-skip gate passed.\n- cargo fmt --all -- --check and git diff --check passed.\n\nAssurance label: native versus direct KVM and CounterTool output/exit/status repeat parity only. This is not L2-log or record/replay parity.\n\nResidual limitation: for a valid directory, KVM may expose host EMFILE because retaining an isolated cwd requires allocating a private descriptor; native fchdir itself does not allocate. This pre-existing backend limitation is not claimed fixed.\n\nPublication state: local prepared work only. PR 611 remains stacked on read-only PR 610 and cannot be published until the prerequisite lands and this recovery is rebased without weakening loginuid/authentication semantics.\n\nNext ranked non-scheduler defect: low-word close and close_range decoding, then missing sendmmsg support." task_id=kvm-lane-to-full-determinism-and-parity
